<BaseLayout title="Safety" description="MedGuard’s safety limits, evidence language, privacy principles and Nigeria emergency guidance.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Safety" title="Know what MedGuard can—and cannot—tell you." description="Safety is not a footer disclaimer. It shapes how the product labels evidence, handles uncertainty and routes urgent situations." />
  <section class="section section--white"><div class="shell prose">
    <div class="emergency-card"><strong>Medical emergency?</strong><p>If someone may be in immediate danger, call Nigeria’s national emergency number <strong>112</strong> and seek urgent medical care. Do not wait for MedGuard or a chatbot response.</p></div>
    <h2>MedGuard is an awareness tool</h2><p>It does not diagnose disease, confirm that a person is ill, prescribe medication, replace clinical examination or guarantee that an area is safe.</p>
    <h2>Evidence language matters</h2><h3>Verified report</h3><p>An attributable official report relevant to a location. It remains linked to its publisher and should still be read in its original context.</p><h3>Projection or risk estimate</h3><p>A modelled outlook based on available signals. It is not an outbreak confirmation and may be incomplete or wrong. Confidence, generation time and validity should accompany the estimate.</p><h3>Environmental context</h3><p>Weather and air quality may support general awareness, but weather alone is not shown as proof of a particular disease.</p>
    <h2>Personal signals have limits</h2><p>Check-in summaries reflect information a user chose to record. They are not medical assessments. Persistent, severe or worsening symptoms need professional evaluation.</p>
    <h2>Official sources, not endorsements</h2><p>MedGuard may reference public information from the <a href="https://ncdc.gov.ng/" rel="external">Nigeria Centre for Disease Control and Prevention</a> and the <a href="https://www.who.int/" rel="external">World Health Organization</a>. Neither reference implies a partnership, approval or endorsement.</p>
    <div class="prose-callout"><strong>When in doubt:</strong> choose professional medical care over an app estimate.</div>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
